VAA1 Evidence Navigation And Authority Model Failure Report
Date: 2026-04-25
Project: VAA1 on Python 1.0 / The-project
Former title: VAA1 BBox/ROI Navigation Bug Fix Report

1. Scope

This report reframes the former BBox/ROI timing bug family as an evidence navigation and
authority model failure across linked timestamped annotations.

The issue was not only that BBoxes or ROI boxes extended, saved, or rendered incorrectly.
The deeper issue was that VAA1 allowed several panels and overlay paths to independently
reconstruct timing, geometry, labels, and visibility for the same evidence item.

The correct fix boundary is therefore architectural:

- every annotation, detection, correction, BBox, ROI box, panel row, and video overlay must be
  treated as a linked timestamped evidence object
- every evidence object must remain navigable from every associated view
- manual correction must be authoritative over automated detection while preserving the original
  detection as provenance and traceback
- when one associated view activates an evidence object, all other associated views must
  synchronize to the same resolved evidence state


2. Correct Architecture

The canonical panel-facing evidence item should be understood as:

Evidence item =

- id
- type
- source kind: detection | manual | correction
- timestamp interval: start/end
- geometry: bbox/roi/keyframes
- semantic labels
- provenance links
- associated panel links

When evidence is selected anywhere, every panel must obey the same rule:

1. resolve evidence id
2. load authoritative evidence state
3. set global active evidence
4. set video time/window from that evidence
5. render BBox/ROI from that evidence
6. update all associated panels from that evidence


3. Authority Rule

The governing authority order is:

manual correction > manual annotation > grouped detection > raw detection

The shorthand remains:

MANUAL CORRECTION WINS EVERYWHERE

However, the mature rule is more specific:

No panel may independently reconstruct timing, geometry, or labels for corrected evidence from
raw detections or grouped spans. Panels may only request the resolved authoritative evidence
object.


4. Correct Bug Framing

The bug family should be named:

Evidence navigation and authority model failure across linked timestamped annotations.

It should not be treated as:

BBox timing bug.

The BBox/ROI symptoms were visible because overlays make authority conflicts obvious, but the
same root problem applies to Objects, OCR, Expressions, Identification, Master Schema, forensic
ROI, and any future annotation-capable panel.


5. Centralized Fix Boundary

The fix should centralize three things:

1. EvidenceAuthorityResolver

   Decides which annotation or detection is authoritative.

2. EvidenceNavigationState

   Stores the active evidence id, active time, active interval, and active geometry.

3. PanelSyncBus / shared hook

   Makes all associated panels react to the same active evidence.

Anything outside this boundary risks patching symptoms while preserving multiple competing
truths.


6. Observed Failures

The following failures were observed during the sprint:

- Extend in threw playback to wrong timestamps, including 0:00.000 and 1:05.000
- Extend in widened internal state without yielding usable slider navigation
- Extend out sometimes widened state without yielding usable future work area
- BBoxes surfaced before their corrected mark-in time
- BBoxes remained visible outside their corrected timespan
- Video panel BBoxes and leaf panel timestamps disagreed
- saved manual timing was ignored by overlay rendering paths
- object-linked manual corrections were re-overridden by grouped/raw track spans
- selected overlays inherited stale draft state from prior edits
- saved leaf panel annotations stayed open after save
- VideoPanel BBox editor stayed open after linked leaf save
- Object save could force a surprise Identification panel focus jump
- timestamped BBox geometry at later frames could overwrite or smear earlier geometry
- a locked forensic/ROI rectangle could persist as a large yellow overlay over unrelated videos
- Tools panel disappeared once due to a frontend crash


7. User Impact

The impact was high:

- analyst trust in the timing system was damaged
- manual validation was blocked
- multiple days were consumed on the same feature family
- the workflow became harder and less predictable after several supposed fixes
- the application behaved as if it had multiple competing clocks
- analysts could not reliably mark one evidence interval and trust it to remain stable


8. Root Cause

This was not one bug. It was a failed authority model.

Too many competing time and geometry sources were allowed to coexist:

1. raw detection timestamp
2. grouped track span
3. saved manual annotation time
4. saved manual geometry keyframes
5. selected editor draft time
6. selected slider scrub state
7. hidden extension workspace/padding state
8. jumpToTime side effects inside extension behavior
9. persistent ROI display state without analysis/time ownership

Because these sources competed, a correction saved in one part of the program could still be
contradicted later by another path during render, navigation, save, or panel synchronization.


9. Wrong Coupling Identified

The system repeatedly showed wrong coupling between:

- overlay key and saved annotation id
- raw track span and corrected manual interval
- track-wide override and time-scoped manual correction
- selected BBox editor state and unrelated panel focus state
- ROI display state and current analysis/video state
- later geometry edits and earlier timestamped geometry

This wrong coupling is why a saved manual correction could appear to not take effect, could
reopen unexpectedly, or could be re-overridden later by unrelated raw timing or geometry.


10. Where Wrong Time Entered The Program

Main leak points identified in the frontend:

A. src/frontend/lib/video-service.ts

- groupDetectedObjectsForDisplay(...)
- grouped object spans using startTimestamp and endTimestamp
- raw/grouped detections feeding panel rows and overlay streams

B. src/frontend/app/V2components/components/panels/VideoPanel.tsx

- buildLocalObjectOverlays(...)
- alignActiveObjectLabelsWithGroupedTracks(...)
- getOverlayTimeBounds(...)
- selectOverlayForEditing(...)
- scrubSelectedOverlayTo(...)
- Extend in/out and selected slider paths
- manual geometry_keyframes merge and resolve path
- lockedForensicRoiBox display path

C. src/frontend/app/V2components/components/panels/OBJDetectionPanel.tsx

- object draft creation from grouped object rows
- object save/close behavior
- linked panel focus behavior

D. src/frontend/app/V2components/components/panels/MasterSchemaPanel.tsx

- leaf save/close behavior
- local correction refresh and panel synchronization behavior


11. Implementation Changes Made

The current remediation introduced or tightened the following:

- added src/frontend/lib/evidence-authority.ts
- defined ResolvedEvidenceItem
- defined EvidenceNavigationState
- defined evidence authority order:
  raw_detection: 10
  grouped_detection: 20
  manual_annotation: 30
  manual_correction: 40
- added resolveManualVisualEvidence(...)
- added resolveDetectedObjectEvidence(...)
- added resolveAuthoritativeEvidence(...)
- added buildEvidenceNavigationState(...)
- updated video navigation helpers to emit resolvedEvidence and navigationState
- added closeManualAnnotationInVideo(...)
- made Master Schema save close the leaf editor and linked VideoPanel editor
- made Object leaf save close the Object editor and linked VideoPanel editor
- removed surprise panel focus jumps from Object save and video BBox save paths
- made VideoPanel listen for videoIndicationEditClose
- made selected BBox/ROI editor close via shared close helper
- changed Extend in behavior into an editable workspace expansion rather than a direct saved
  interval mutation
- removed jumpToTime side effects from Extend in/out behavior
- added one-drag slider framing for the selected BBox/ROI interval
- preserved selected overlays inside the expanded edit workspace
- fixed object-backed save to load existing manual annotation keyframes before adding a new
  timestamped geometry keyframe
- bounded geometry interpolation so later BBoxes cannot smear across cuts or distant timestamps
- scoped locked forensic ROI overlays to videoId and timestamp
- cleared stale locked ROI overlays when native annotation/OCR annotation workflows open


12. Analyst-Facing Behavior Now Required

From the analyst perspective, the intended BBox/ROI interaction is one workflow:

1. open a detection or saved evidence item
2. use Extend in to add X seconds of editable workspace before and after the item
3. drag the slider across the actual area of interest in time
4. resize or reposition the BBox/ROI as needed at the relevant timestamp
5. choose or adjust the label
6. save
7. the editor closes
8. the BBox/ROI appears only inside the saved interval
9. timestamped geometry remains stable at every saved timestamp
10. reopening restores the saved correction

Extend in/out is not the feature. The feature is fast temporal drawing of the evidence interval.


13. Timestamp And Geometry Rule

The timestamp/coordinates regime must hold without excuses:

- a BBox/ROI coordinate set belongs to a specific analysis/video
- a BBox/ROI coordinate set belongs to a specific timestamp or keyframe
- saving a later geometry adjustment must not eat or smear an earlier keyframe
- manual geometry may interpolate only over short, continuous gaps
- geometry must not interpolate freely across cuts or distant timestamps
- stale ROI display state must not render on unrelated videos or unrelated timestamps


14. Panel Synchronization Rule

Every annotation-capable panel must follow the same operating principle:

- selecting evidence resolves the authoritative evidence state
- save commits analyst evidence
- save closes the active editor
- linked video editor closes when the linked leaf editor saves
- automated evidence is preserved as provenance, not as override
- no panel may steal focus unless the analyst explicitly requested that navigation
- reopening must restore saved state, not stale draft state

This has been proven for key Master Schema and Object save paths, and partially enforced for
shared video navigation. It still needs a full global panel alignment sweep.


15. Expressions Clarification

Expressions must not be governed by a flat primal list of emotions as the primary analyst model.

Automatic expression samples may remain as raw evidence. Manual Expressions should follow the
genre-weighted interpretation model and remain analyst evidence beside automatic scoring, not a
replacement for it.

The Expressions test should therefore verify:

- automatic expression samples remain visible as automated evidence
- manual genre-weighted Expressions annotations can be added
- manual expression evidence appears in Master Schema
- raw expression scoring is preserved
- save/open/close behavior follows the same panel synchronization rule


16. Verification Added

Governance checks were expanded in:

src/frontend/tests/manual-annotation-governance.test.mjs

The current governance regime now checks:

- manual categories align across type, video UI, and Tools navigation
- every manual category has subcategory support
- every manual category has a Master Schema leaf panel
- forensic ROI intent options align across Tools and Video
- Objects remains a leaf, not the master schema sink
- manual BBox geometry stays timestamp scoped
- manual annotation panels use shared video navigation helpers
- detection and analysis panels use shared video seek navigation
- linked evidence authority is centralized before panel navigation
- timestamped overlay geometry stays scoped to one analysis and timestamp

Latest verification:

- npm run test:governance passed 12/12
- npx tsc --noEmit passed


17. Remaining Risk

The current implementation is a root-readiness pass, not the final polished UX.

Remaining risks:

- the BBox/ROI UI is still primitive and too button-heavy
- slider interaction works at a primal level but needs a cleaner analyst-facing design
- all panels still need a complete save/open/close alignment sweep
- OCR and Expressions manual annotation flows need end-to-end manual tests
- timestamped ROI/BBox behavior needs repeated cross-cut manual tests
- the PanelSyncBus/shared hook architecture is not yet fully realized as a single hook
- some resolver logic is still panel-facing rather than fully app-global


18. Recommended Next Phase

The next phase should stay inside the fix boundary:

1. finish the shared evidence authority/navigation hook
2. make all annotation-capable panels consume resolved authoritative evidence
3. remove remaining panel-local reconstruction of corrected timing, geometry, and labels
4. simplify BBox/ROI UI around one fast analyst action:
   draw the time span, adjust the box, label it, save
5. manually test one path at a time:
   Master Schema
   Objects
   OCR
   Expressions
   Identification
   BBox/ROI cross-cut geometry
6. keep raw/grouped detections only for fallback and traceback once manual correction exists


19. Bottom Line

The former BBox/ROI navigation problem was a symptom.

The actual failure was evidence navigation and authority model instability across linked
timestamped annotations.

The corrected governing rule is:

VAA1 treats annotations, detections, corrections, BBoxes, ROI boxes, panel rows, and video
overlays as linked timestamped evidence objects.

Every evidence object must remain navigable from every associated view.

Manual correction is authoritative over automated detection while preserving the original
detection as provenance and traceback.

When one associated view activates an evidence object, all other associated views must
synchronize to the same resolved evidence state.

That is the fix boundary. Anything else is patching symptoms.
